{"name":"Germander Speedwell","hex":"#0094c8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"germander","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Mediterranean herb, of species Teucrium chamaedrys, historically grown for medicinal use but now mostly as an ornamental miniature hedge in herb gardens.","Any plant of the genus Teucrium, some with small, pink, white, or pale purple flowers and a small upper lip."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/germander"},{"term":"speedwell","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the genus Veronica"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/speedwell"}],"entries":[{"title":"Veronica chamaedrys","blocks":[{"text":"Veronica chamaedrys, the germander speedwell, bird's-eye speedwell, or cat's eyes, is a herbaceous perennial species of flowering plant in the plantain family Plantaginaceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Ehrenpreis-JR-T20-2021-05-29.jpg/330px-Ehrenpreis-JR-T20-2021-05-29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Veronica_chamaedrys","wikidata":"Q157343"},{"title":"Teucrium","blocks":[{"text":"Teucrium is a cosmopolitan genus of flowering plants in the mint family Lamiaceae, commonly known as germanders. Plants in this genus are perennial herbs or shrubs, with branches that are more or less square in cross-section, leaves arranged in opposite pairs, and flowers arranged in thyrses, the corolla with mostly white to cream-coloured, lobed petals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Teucrium_eremaeum_-_Flickr_-_Kevin_Thiele.jpg/330px-Teucrium_eremaeum_-_Flickr_-_Kevin_Thiele.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teucrium","wikidata":"Q157714"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Veronica_chamaedrys_Aberystwyth_2024_Leaf.jp